of distinct color events

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:05.900
that have happened over
the past 30 minutes,

00:20:05.900 --> 00:20:09.650
over the past 2 days,
and over the past 7 days?

00:20:09.650 --> 00:20:12.290
The next question is,
what are the number

00:20:12.290 --> 00:20:16.340
of distinct colors that
occurred in the last minute

00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:18.270
for the past 30 minutes?

00:20:18.270 --> 00:20:20.870
And finally, we're
going to have a chart

00:20:20.870 --> 00:20:23.060
that we are going to use
to monitor the ingestion

00:20:23.060 --> 00:20:25.700
latency of how long it's
actually taking to process

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:28.070
these events from user
actions to it being

00:20:28.070 --> 00:20:30.780
available in the data warehouse.

00:20:30.780 --> 00:20:33.500
So this is a high level
architecture diagram

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:36.650
essentially expanding
on what components we're

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:38.640
going to be looking at today.

00:20:38.640 --> 00:20:41.007
So on the left hand
side, the yellow box--

00:20:41.007 --> 00:20:41.840
it's a little faint.

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:45.080
Sorry about that-- the left hand
box represents the same side

00:20:45.080 --> 00:20:47.610
that we just saw previously.

00:20:47.610 --> 00:20:49.460
So we can see here,
Cloud Firestore

00:20:49.460 --> 00:20:52.640
is sort of the bridging
point into the rest of GCP

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:54.680
that we're going to be
integrating with today.

00:20:54.680 --> 00:20:56.510
And we're going
to specifically be

00:20:56.510 --> 00:21:01.160
using Cloud Functions to
monitor change events on each

00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:04.670
of the pixel documents
inside the database.

00:21:04.670 --> 00:21:06.500
When each of those
events is triggered,

00:21:06.500 --> 00:21:09.170
we're going to
handle that event,

00:21:09.170 --> 00:21:12.650
process it, and feed that
into BigQuery that will then

00:21:12.650 --> 00:21:19.010
be used to generate some
predefined views to feed charts

00:21:19.010 --> 00:21:21.080
inside Data Studio
so that we can put up

00:21:21.080 --> 00:21:24.470
a dashboard in our office for
everybody to able to look at.

00:21:24.470 --> 00:21:27.170
And since Cloud
Functions are these kind

00:21:27.170 --> 00:21:29.870
of magic, ephemeral
things, we need

00:21:29.870 --> 00:21:32.060
to have some monitoring for us.

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:34.040
So we're going to
leverage Stackdriver

00:21:34.040 --> 00:21:36.380
to do essentially
metrics monitoring

00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:39.940
and invocations per second,
and those sorts of things

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:41.150
over time.

