00:27:56.650 --> 00:28:00.030
So the service account gives
your function an identity

00:28:00.030 --> 00:28:04.830
as far as access
controls and security are

00:28:04.830 --> 00:28:07.350
concerned in the greater GCP.

00:28:07.350 --> 00:28:10.320
So when I'm integrating
with BigQuery,

00:28:10.320 --> 00:28:14.820
the identity of next IO
storage service account

00:28:14.820 --> 00:28:18.300
is given the permission
to write into BigQuery.

00:28:18.300 --> 00:28:21.210
So if you've got many
projects or many teams,

00:28:21.210 --> 00:28:24.570
you can do fine-grain controls
to where you could say,

00:28:24.570 --> 00:28:27.390
this function is able to write
to this thing in BigQuery,

00:28:27.390 --> 00:28:30.780
but this other function is
only able to interact with GCS.

00:28:30.780 --> 00:28:32.550
So it gives you
that kind of control

00:28:32.550 --> 00:28:36.540
to be able to handle multiple
things at the same time.

00:28:36.540 --> 00:28:38.520
So jumping over
