00:32:51.772 --> 00:32:53.230
So this is one of
the things that's

00:32:53.230 --> 00:32:56.040
really powerful about Cloud
Functions is it essentially

00:32:56.040 --> 00:32:59.330
takes care of all of the
scaling factors for you.

00:32:59.330 --> 00:33:02.470
So by us triggering
events and events being in

00:33:02.470 --> 00:33:06.460
cued to be processed,
GCP figures out

00:33:06.460 --> 00:33:09.680
how many functions it
needs to scale up for you,

00:33:09.680 --> 00:33:12.797
and when they can be able
to scale down, and back up,

00:33:12.797 --> 00:33:13.880
and those sorts of things.

00:33:13.880 --> 00:33:16.510
So that's why you're
seeing some spikiness this

00:33:16.510 --> 00:33:19.420
